IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei6-schedule-rows`
IMPORT `ei6-schedule-v`

-- Tests of Schedule V (src:3496-3540). Expected values are read off the printed table by hand: the row is the hours of
-- insurable employment, the column the band of the regional rate of unemployment, counted from the left (1 = "6% and under").

§ `Schedule V - Table of Weeks of Benefits - Seasonal Workers`

-- Row 420-454 (src:3500): eight blank cells, then 31, 33, 35, 37.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 420 (13.5%) EQUALS JUST 31
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 420 (14.5%) EQUALS JUST 33
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 420 (15.5%) EQUALS JUST 35
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 420 (20%) EQUALS JUST 37
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 420 (12.5%) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Row 455-489 (src:3501): 29 in the eighth column.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 455 (12.5%) EQUALS JUST 29
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 454 (12.5%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 454.5 (12.5%) EQUALS NOTHING
-- No row below 420 hours.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 419 (20%) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Row 700-734 (src:3508): 19, 21, ... 41.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 700 (5%) EQUALS JUST 19
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 734 (6%) EQUALS JUST 19
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 734 (6.01%) EQUALS JUST 21
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 700 (20%) EQUALS JUST 41
-- Row 1400-1434 (src:3528): 29, 31, 33, 35, 37, 39, 41, 43, 45, 45, 45, 45. Row 1435-1469 (src:3529): 30, 32, ...
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 1400 (5%) EQUALS JUST 29
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 1434 (8.5%) EQUALS JUST 35
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 1434 (13.5%) EQUALS JUST 45
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 1435 (5%) EQUALS JUST 30
-- Row 1785-1819 (src:3539): 40, 42, 44, 45, ... Last row 1820 and more (src:3540): 41, 43, 45, 45, ...
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 1819 (5%) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 1819.5 (5%) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 1820 (5%) EQUALS JUST 41
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 1820 (6.5%) EQUALS JUST 43
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 1820 (7.5%) EQUALS JUST 45
#ASSERT `Act Schedule V the maximum number of weeks of benefits for seasonal workers` 3000 (5%) EQUALS JUST 41
